(1) Root Cause: The capability `emsweb-emsenn0-autonomous-daily` is reporting a configuration error (`exit 78/CONFIG`) triggered by a `source-reconciliation-refused` conflict within the NotebookLM integration, as documented at `lib/emsenn/services/561-group/services/board-of-directors/services/executive-office/services/leader-movement-team/data/state/capability-registry.json:1602`. The discrepancy exists between the path requested in the work order (`lib/emsenn/services/561-group/services/rsc-quiescent/services/emsweb/services/youtube-channel-enterprise`) and the existing service path naming conventions observed in the registry, which appear to use prefixed identifiers (e.g., `modern-business-youtube-channel-enterprise` at line 441).

(2) Repair Proposal:
*   Standardize the target path to match the enterprise naming convention observed in `lib/emsenn/services/561-group/services/board-of-directors/services/executive-office/services/leader-movement-team/data/state/capability-registry.json` by updating the path to `lib/emsenn/services/561-group/services/rsc-quiescent/services/emsweb/services/youtube-channel-enterprise` (assuming identity reconciliation is intended) or creating the missing directory structure at that path.
*   Resolve the `prior-source-receipt-conflict` by removing any stale source lock files associated with `emsweb-emsenn0-autonomous-daily` in the systemd-managed environment.
*   Update `data/state/capability-registry.json` to change the `status` field for `emsweb-emsenn0-autonomous-daily` from `BROKEN` to `RUNNING_VERIFIED`.
*   Execute the verification command: `journalctl --user -u emsweb-emsenn0-autonomous-daily.service -n 15`.

(3) Unknown: The specific technical payload of the "source-receipt" that caused the reconciliation conflict is unknown; the registry error provides only the exception type, not the contents of the conflicting source material.

